nc-name">Peoria</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Peoria were one of the main peoples of the Illinois Confederation, living along the Illinois river, where the city of Peoria bears their name.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pepi-i"><span class="enc-name">Pepi I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pepi I Meryre was a pharaoh of the Sixth Dynasty of Egypt whose long reign was one of the most active of the Old Kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pepi-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pepi-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pepi II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pepi II was a pharaoh of the Sixth Dynasty of Egypt, credited by tradition with one of the longest reigns in history, of up to 90 years.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pepin-i-of-aquitaine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pepin-i-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pepin I of Aquitaine</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pepin I of Aquitaine was a son of the Carolingian emperor Louis the Pious and king of Aquitaine from 817 until his death in 838.</span></a></li></ul>
